course: dictionary
lesson: 12965
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «The executive ran the company from a tall office.» Here an executive is a person with an important job who makes decisions and manages others.
explain: Executive can also describe a thing, so it is an adjective. «She flew home in executive class.» Executive class means seats and travel made for important managers, often expensive. Here executive is not a person at all.
explain: In citizenship lessons, executive names a part of government. «The executive carries out the laws.» Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then check by putting your meaning in place of the word.
fact: Executive can be a noun (an executive) or an adjective (executive).
fact: «An executive» is a person with an important job in a company who makes decisions and manages others.
fact: «Executive class» describes things made for important managers, often expensive.
fact: In citizenship, the executive is one branch of government, along with the law-makers and the courts.
fact: Phrases to know: «chief executive» and «executive decision».
exercise: «The executive picked the new team for the project.» What is an executive here? | A type of shoe | *A person with an important job who makes decisions | A word for a school bell | A small animal that lives in water
exercise: «Dad flew home in executive class, with big seats and extra space.» What does executive describe here? | Sad and quiet feelings | A kind of weather | *Travel made for important managers, often expensive | Something very cheap and small
exercise: In citizenship class, Ruby learns that the executive is one branch of government. What does the executive do? | Only tells the weather each day | Counts the money in a bank | *Runs the country and carries out the laws | Sells food in the market
test: «The chief executive made the final choice for the company.» What is a chief executive? | A fast runner in a race | A flying machine | *The most important manager of a company | A sort of hat
test: «The executive branch makes sure the laws are carried out.» What does executive mean in «the executive branch»? | Expensive and posh | A person who sells cars | A large room for meetings | *The part of government that runs the country
exam: «Our executive decides what the company will make next.» Which meaning fits? | Seats made for important managers | A kind of cake | Part of a government that makes laws | *A person with an important job who makes decisions
